# URL where the backend (packing_organiser/backend) is reachable from your
# PHONE, not from this machine. "localhost" only works when running in a web
# browser on the same machine as the backend.
#
# - Expo Go on a physical phone via a Codespaces-forwarded port: use the
#   Codespaces "Ports" tab HTTPS forwarding URL for port 3000 (and make sure
#   that port's visibility is set to Public).
# - Expo Go on a physical phone on the same Wi-Fi as a locally-run backend:
#   use your computer's LAN IP, e.g. http://192.168.1.23:3000
# - iOS Simulator on the same Mac as a locally-run backend: http://localhost:3000
# - Android Emulator on the same machine as a locally-run backend: http://10.0.2.2:3000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
